{"id": 52, "ts": 1784132416.57196, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate the point that B\u2019s alleged weak memory for numbers remains unverified, so it shouldn\u2019t dominate our assessment.\u202fHowever, the concerns we do have about B\u2014being perceived as pretentious and sometimes using the wrong tone\u2014directly touch on crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication, which are critical in a long\u2011haul cockpit.\u202fIn contrast, A\u2019s record shows 100\u202f% operational reliability, calmness under pressure, and rapid correct decision\u2011making, but his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious questions about his adaptability, feedback orientation, and long\u2011distance responsibility.\u202fBecause we have no concrete evidence of A\u2019s leadership maturity or ability to grow with the role, I remain convinced that B\u2019s overall profile\u2014strong reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence\u2014offers a more balanced fit despite the communication issues, which we can address through targeted training.\u202fI therefore keep my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB, while agreeing that we should still seek reliability and stress\u2011handling data for Candidate\u202fC before any final decision."}
